 Git Source Represents an async order for a swap in the Uniswap V4 pool. struct AsyncOrder {
    PoolKey key;
    address owner;
    bool zeroForOne;
    uint256 amountIn;
    uint256 amountOutMin;
    uint256 priorityFee;
    uint160 sqrtPrice;
    bytes32 salt;
} Properties NameTypeDescriptionkeyPoolKeyThe Uniswap V4 PoolKey identifying the pool the order is placed against.owneraddressThe maker who supplied amountIn of the input currency at order submission.zeroForOneboolDirection of the order. true => input is currency0, output is currency1.amountInuint256Amount of input currency the maker escrowed. Direct matching may partially fill it;unused input is returned when the maker's minimum output is satisfied.amountOutMinuint256Minimum amount of output currency the maker accepts. The implicit limit price isamountOutMin / amountIn. A filler or direct match must satisfy the live minimumfor the amount it consumes.priorityFeeuint256Non-refundable USDC bid for equal-price priority: at least $0.10, or 0.1% of theorder's USDC notional when that is less. Matched portions, and the remainder on afill, cancel or dust closure, go to the protocol FeeVault.sqrtPriceuint160Sqrt-price limit passed to PoolManager.swap on submission. The hook consumesthe whole input in beforeSwap, so the pool never trades against it.saltbytes32Contract-assigned salt that disambiguates orders. The hook computes this at createtime from keccak256(timestamp, block.number, msg.sender, owner, amountIn,<br/>amountOutMin, priorityFee) and emits it in AsyncOrderCreated so the maker can reference theorder in cancel / updatePrice. Submitters pass bytes32(0) on create — the valuein this slot is only read on cancel / updatePrice / fill paths.

